findings.body:
**The committed-`node_modules` guard checks only one level, but the JSDoc and decision 81 promise it checks everything inside.**

```ts
const linksOut =
  escapes(local) || readdirSync(local).some((name) => escapes(join(local, name)));
```

`readdirSync(local)` lists only the top-level names, and in a committed tree `.bin/`, `@scope/` and `<pkg>/` are real directories. Their realpath stays inside the checkout, so the guard passes, and nothing below them is checked.

Suppose a branch commits `node_modules/.bin/vitest` (mode `120000`) with an absolute target in the session's worktree:

- the guard passes and `linkEnvironment` returns at L346 with the committed directory kept, so the main checkout's packages are not linked in;
- the test stage (`pnpm run test`, cwd = checkout) resolves `vitest` through that link, to a file the live session can rewrite while the stage runs;
- the sandbox allows reads by default (`sandbox-profile.utils.ts:123-125`), so the worktree is readable;
- the scope audit runs only after build, test and lint. It blocks the merge only when scope-in does not cover `node_modules/**`.

This delta introduced the gap: at 1f4adeb every committed `node_modules` was refused, and now the directory is kept after a top-level check. The JSDoc (L324-326) and decision 81 (`docs/09-decisions.md` L4154-4155) both say "unless something in it links outside the checkout", a guarantee the code doesn't provide.

The delta also keeps a vendored regular-file `.bin/vitest`, so a deliberately malicious session has other ways to fake a pass. Either make the check match the stated guarantee, or narrow the wording to what is checked and record the rest as part of the ceiling.

**Fix direction:** before any stage, resolve every mode-`120000` entry in the pinned tree once (`git ls-tree -r -z <sha>`) and refuse any that resolves outside the checkout. A recursive `readdirSync` of `node_modules` alone doesn't close it: `.bin -> ../tools/bin`, with `tools/bin/vitest` pointing into the worktree, would still pass.

